# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*

# Python virtual environment
.venv/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# temp workspaces
#
# The sandbox is scratch, WITH TWO EXCEPTIONS. Ruled 2026-08-03: the minimal
# case is a sandbox-only test bed whose entire output is (a) the emitted prompt
# and (b) the transcript. Those are the evidence for the part-context evolution
# design discussions, and evidence that only exists on disk cannot be diffed
# circle against circle, and dies to a `git clean`.
#
# `work/sandbox/*` rather than `work/sandbox/`, deliberately: git
# cannot re-include anything beneath an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so a `!` line under
# the directory form would silently do nothing. Excluding the children instead
# leaves the directory itself readable, and the two negations below then apply.
# Moved from coordinator/sandbox/, R176, 2026-08-15 — coordinator/ is product
# domain and this is transcript-derived content.
# A MEMO, NOT A RECORD. work/token_counts.json holds sha256 -> token count
# for prompt prefixes the model service has already counted (R260,
# 2026-08-20). It makes no claim about this project — losing it costs one
# re-count and nothing else — and it would otherwise churn in every diff
# whenever a practice, a briefing or a distillate moved.
work/token_counts.json
work/sandbox/*
!work/sandbox/prompts/
!work/sandbox/circles/
work/nightly/

# Tool working databases — rewritten constantly, ~11MB each time
.fileintel/

# Run logs — derived, one per run
work/logs/nightly*.log

# TWO MEMOS, NOT RECORDS — 2026-08-26. Both are written by a live circle,
# both were tracked by nothing, and so both sat dirty in the working tree
# forever after: enough, in the lab, to deadlock a `pull-main`, which
# refuses a dirty tree. Ignored rather than committed because each is
# superseded by something that IS the record, and neither loses anything
# by staying untracked — they are read off local disk, never out of git:
#   closing_<OT>.json  the START-OF-CLOSE marker. mark_close_started():
#                      "IT IS NEVER DELETED. A close report supersedes it",
#                      and close_<OT>.json beside it is committed.
#   dream_<OT>.json    phase 2's run marker. The `dream/<OT>` git tag is
#                      the evidence a circle was processed; the file is
#                      already_processed()'s second reader, kept for the
#                      tree where git cannot answer at all (R349), and
#                      still on disk there whether git tracks it or not.
# The registers a circle writes — self/working_sets.toml, self/proposals.toml
# — are the opposite case and are STAGED by the close now, not ignored.
#
# `dream_[0-9]*` AND NOT `dream_*`: dream_error_<OT>.json is a FAILURE REPORT,
# a real diagnostic naming what refused and how to re-run, and it stays
# visible on purpose. inter_circle.py globs the run marker the same way, for
# the same reason.
work/logs/closing_*.json
work/logs/dream_[0-9]*.json

# Temp workspaces — staging, caches, locks, snapshots
work/issue_trial/

# Claude Code CLI's own scheduler lock — rewritten by the harness itself,
# not project content
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Temp workspaces — staging, caches, locks, snapshots
work/circle_audit/

# Run logs — derived, one per run
work/logs/circle_audit*.log
